################ A silent alert - found and fixed ################
# The first version of the CPU alert filtered on the `container` label:
$ sum(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{namespace="demo", container="podinfo"}[1m]))
   NO DATA (empty result)

# Why: on k3s with the Docker runtime (cri-dockerd), cAdvisor reports POD-level
# cgroups only. The real label set has no `container` label at all:
$ container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{namespace="demo"}
   {'cpu': 'total', 'id': '/kubepods/burstable/pod2b9aef83-...', 'job': 'kubelet', 'pod': 'podinfo-74bf7d9db9-cvbzg'}
   {'cpu': 'total', 'id': '/kubepods/burstable/podbb6a196c-...', 'job': 'kubelet', 'pod': 'podinfo-74bf7d9db9-5cc4h'}

# An alert on an empty expression does NOT error. It shows "inactive" forever,
# indistinguishable from a healthy system - so it would never have fired.

# Fixed: filter on `pod` instead
$ sum(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{namespace="demo", pod=~"podinfo-.*"}[1m]))
   0.0007 cores
